# Who reviews what.
#
# One maintainer today, so every path lists the same person. The value of the file is not the
# distribution of work: it is that "who is accountable for this path" has an answer that does not
# depend on someone being online. Add narrower rules here when a second maintainer takes a subsystem.
#
# What this file does NOT do by itself: GitHub only consults it when `main` has branch protection
# with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled. That setting is currently OFF -- checked against the
# API, `main` reports "Branch not protected" -- so today this file records ownership and nothing
# more. Turning it on is a repository settings change, which is why the gap is written down here
# instead of being assumed away.

